      "id": "clm_01M4VYR28WR1MKM36DCYM6BYRZ",
      "statement": "The son of Joiada who married Sanballat's daughter (Neh 13:28) is the Manasseh whom Josephus places under Darius III.",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": "Neh.13.28",
      "classification": "disputed",
      "reasoning": "Keil and Cowley both identify the incidents and attribute Josephus's setting to his chronological errors (he calls Sanballat's sender \"Darius, the last king\", makes Manasseh a brother of Jaddua, and has Sanballat die in 332, though his sons acted for him by 408). Older theologians and Petermann (as reported by Keil) proposed a second Sanballat with a second marriage. Josephus himself (read directly) sets the marriage in the reign of Darius III.",
